bin/
tmp/
dist/
/yomihon
/yomihon.exe
.env
.DS_Store
# Frontend tools install under .github/; ignore dependency trees at any depth.
# The product build and Go package graph need no Node.
node_modules/
# A clean clone receives the code, its build inputs, the judge rule inventory,
# the record of what yomihon does to the person running it, and the documents a
# contributor needs to work here: how to build and test it, what a pull request
# must contain, and what an agent opening one may and may not touch. The
# maintainer's own process, authoring, and design notes stay on the maintainer's
# machine, out of history. Each redistributed asset carries its licence text
# beside it under assets/.
# tests/ holds local harness self-tests; yomihon's Go tests live in
# internal/*_test.go.
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.lsp.json
tests/
/AGENT_INTERFACE.md
/AUTHORING.md
/CLAUDE.md
/ENGINEERING_STANDARD.md
/ENGINEERING_STANDARD.sha256
/PROJECT_PROFILE.md
/docs/*
!/docs/judge-rules.md
# The privacy inventory and the threat model state the software's behaviour
# toward the person running it, which is the claim a stranger checks the code
# against; the rest of docs/ is the history of how the work was decided and
# stays out. These are directories rather than files because git does not walk
# into an excluded directory, so a file inside one cannot be re-included on its
# own — which also means anything added under either directory ships.
!/docs/privacy/
!/docs/security/
/.github/CODEOWNERS
